### ❌ pull_request_target reaches job test → … → 🔑 AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY

\`pull_request_target reaches job test\` → \`.github/workflows/ci.yml#test\` → \`AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\`

- **why:** Job .github/workflows/ci.yml#test is triggered by untrusted input (pull_request_target) and runs PR code at .github/workflows/ci.yml:7 while holding credential AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, which that code can read and exfiltrate.
- **fix:** Remove AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY from the untrusted-triggerable job .github/workflows/ci.yml#test, or restrict its triggers to trusted events.
- **sink:** credential \`AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\`
- **at:** \`.github/workflows/ci.yml:7\` → \`AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\`
