exports[`composeReport (KTD7) > snapshots the real incident fixtures > untrusted-text-shell 1`] = `
"Blastgate: reachable attacker-controlled path to a secret in acme/widgets reaches DEPLOY_KEY at .github/workflows/triage.yml:12

## Blastgate automated security report

This is an automated report from Blastgate, a scanner for attacker-to-secret paths in CI workflows. It is limited to proven paths: Blastgate only reports a fail when it can trace a reachable path from attacker-controllable input to a secret or credential in \`acme/widgets\`.

1 reachable path found. Each lists where the input enters, what it reaches, why, and how to break the path. How the scanner decides what is reportable: https://github.com/jwolberg/blastgate/blob/main/docs/threat-model.md

**How to respond:** if this is accurate, breaking any edge on a path (the fix lines below) closes it. If it is wrong, or you accept the risk, reply here or close this report to decline; no further report will be filed for these findings.

**Disclosure:** we suggest a 90-day coordinated-disclosure window from the date of this report. Blastgate does not publish this finding; any advisory is yours to publish.

---

### ❌ untrusted issues text reaches job triage (github.event.issue.title) → … → 🔑 DEPLOY_KEY

\`untrusted issues text reaches job triage (github.event.issue.title)\` → \`.github/workflows/triage.yml#triage\` → \`DEPLOY_KEY\`

- **why:** untrusted issues text reaches job triage (github.event.issue.title) — job .github/workflows/triage.yml#triage expands attacker-written event text with '\${{ }}' directly into code the job runs (a 'run:' shell script or 'github-script'), before that code starts. Text that closes the surrounding quote or string runs as code in the job, which holds credential DEPLOY_KEY and can send it out.
- **fix:** Pass the text through an environment variable and use it quoted ('env: VAR: \${{ … }}' then '"$VAR"') instead of expanding '\${{ }}' inside the script; remove DEPLOY_KEY from the untrusted-triggered job .github/workflows/triage.yml#triage if it is not needed there.
- **sink:** credential \`DEPLOY_KEY\`
- **at:** \`.github/workflows/triage.yml:12\` → \`DEPLOY_KEY\`
- **OWASP:** \`ASI01:2026\`, \`MCP10:2025\`

---

_Scanned by Blastgate 0.1.0 at commit \`aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaab\`._"
`;
